<robot name="ds_fetch">

  <link name="root">
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00" ixy="0.00" ixz="0.00" iyy="0.00" iyz="0.00" izz="0.00"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>
  <link name="root_arm_1_link_1">
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00" ixy="0.00" ixz="0.00" iyy="0.00" iyz="0.00" izz="0.00"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>
  <link name="root_arm_1_link_2">
    <inertial>
      <mass value="0"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00" ixy="0.00" ixz="0.00" iyy="0.00" iyz="0.00" izz="0.00"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>
  <joint name="root_x_axis_joint" type="prismatic">
    <parent link="root"/>
    <child link="root_arm_1_link_1"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <limit effort="100" lower="-20" upper="20" velocity="0.50"/>
    <dynamics damping="10.0" friction="10"/>
  </joint>
  <joint name="root_y_axis_joint" type="prismatic">
    <parent link="root_arm_1_link_1"/>
    <child link="root_arm_1_link_2"/>
    <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
    <limit effort="100" lower="-20" upper="20" velocity="0.50"/>
    <dynamics damping="10.0" friction="10"/>
  </joint>
  <joint name="root_z_rotation_joint" type="revolute">
    <parent link="root_arm_1_link_2"/>
    <child link="base_link"/>
    <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
    <dynamics damping="1.0" />
    <!-- K58: was +-6.28, i.e. exactly one revolution each way, and that is an
         artefact rather than a physical stop. This is the *virtual* joint that models
         a mobile base's planar spin; a real differential-drive base turns as many
         times as it likes. The bound exists only because mplib refuses a `continuous`
         joint ("continuous revolute joint"), the same reason the three arm roll joints
         were declared revolute at one revolution and later widened.

         The cost of the old bound was a live defect (K54 / D14): `rotate_base_z`
         always takes the locally short way and nothing tracks accumulated heading, so
         a plant -> bucket -> plant round sums past 2*pi, the joint lands on the stop,
         and every later turn plays its whole trapezoid into it, moves the base by
         thousandths of a radian and *returns success* — after which the oracle drives
         on a heading it does not have. Measured on the 30-seed fleet: 21 of 30 seeds
         reach -6.28 during the trip-1 plant drive and survive only because some later
         turn happens to be positive and unwinds them; seed 48 is the one where it did
         not, and it failed `drive to plant 2` with dyaw 163.4 deg at all three rungs.

         Widening is preferred over the parked long-way-round fix (TODOS "the base
         winds onto its joint stop") because that one *adds* rotation by construction,
         and this branch is also trying to make trajectories shorter, not longer.
         +-50 rad is ~8 revolutions: bounded, so mplib is happy, and unreachable inside
         a 5200-step episode (the worst fleet case commands -20.31 rad).

         Nothing rescales: the base is driven by PDBaseForwardVelControllerConfig with
         hardcoded lower=[-1,-3.14]/upper=[1,3.14] (ds_fetch.py:217-224), a *velocity*
         controller whose action mapping does not read this position limit. -->
    <limit effort="33.82" lower="-50.0" upper="50.0" velocity="1.256"/>
  </joint>

